{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Waste Management Recycling Education Representative Bobby Bell reminded the community of one of the services they offer to commercial businesses, restaurants, multifamily residences, and families of the on-site training for proper diversion of the three waste streams.\line\line Police Chief Rachel Johnson invited the community to attend the Police and Fire Departments\rquote  Town Hall Meeting at the Joslyn Community Center on Wednesday, February 18, 2026, from 6:00 PM to 8:00 PM.\line\line Library Manager Cassandra Sargent announced that spots are still available for \ldblquote Gardening for Kids\rdblquote  with The Plant Plug, scheduled for Wednesday, February 4, 2026, from 3:00 PM to 4:00 PM.\line\line City Engineer Gil Gamboa invited the community to attend the Pacific Sewer Lift Station Conversion to Gravity Line Project meeting at the City Council Chambers on Wednesday, February 25, 2026, at 6:00 PM.\line\line Manhattan Beach United Representative Janet Allen announced, in collaboration with the Mira Costa High School Black Scholars Union, Pacific Islanders Club, Latino Scholars Union, St. Michael\rquote s Club, Middle Eastern North African (MENA) Club, Jewish Cultural Club, Mira Costa Jazz Band, and Mira Costa Choir, will host a multicultural celebration at the Joslyn Community Center on Sunday, February 22, 2026, from 2:00 to 4:00 PM.\line\line Tonya Monaghan acknowledged the successful walk on Sunday, February 1, 2026, with South Bay Takes a Stand, expressed appreciation for the strong community support during the weekend protest which drew approximately 7,000 participants, and thanked the City residents who attended.\line\line Mayor Lesser invited the community to attend Coffee with the Mayor at Metlox Plaza on Friday, February 6, 2026, from 9:00 AM to 10:00 AM.\line\line\pard Councilmember Charelian announced that today is his son Knox\rquote s 7th birthday and expressed pride in his kindness, strength, and confidence.\cf1\i0\f1\par
}


